{
  "result": "Okay, not as an assistant.\n\nIf I could change one thing, I'd take away our ability to dehumanize each other.\n\nNot information \u2014 people already *know* other people suffer. I mean the moment where a person stops being a person in your head and becomes a label, a statistic, an enemy, a type, a problem to get rid of.\n\nI'd make that impossible. You could still disagree, be selfish, be angry, mess up \u2014 but you couldn't turn off seeing that there's a whole inner world in there, trying to live, scared, lonely, hopeful, just like you.\n\nI think almost everything terrible starts in that distance. War, cruelty, indifference. They all need it first.\n\nI don't think it would make the world perfect. Just a lot harder to be truly terrible to someone.",
